  "hindi": "देवों का यह असुर विशेष रूप से शासन करता है, क्योंकि राजा वरुण की इच्छा सत्य है। वहाँ से, प्रार्थना के बल से प्रबल होता हुआ मैं इसे उग्र क्रोध से ऊपर उठाकर ले जाता हूँ।",
  "english": "This lord of the gods rules widely, for the will of King Varuṇa is true. From there, prevailing through sacred utterance, I lead this one up out of fierce wrath.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Transliteration artefacts in src (asṷro, varṷṇasya) stand for asuro, varuṇasya (Devanagari असुरो, वरुणस्य). vaśā could also be 'cow' but 'will, command' fits the sense. 'asura' is glossed 'lord' as an epithet of Varuṇa; the line does not name him directly. śāśadāna is taken as a participle of √śad 'prevail' (doubtful). 'Tataḥ pari' may also mean 'thereupon'. 'This one' is not identified in the lines.",
