  "hindi": "हे राजन् वरुण, तुम्हारे क्रोध को नमस्कार हो; हे उग्र, तुमने सारे द्रोह को देख लिया है। मैं हज़ार दूसरों को साथ-साथ आगे भेजता हूँ; तुम्हारा यह जन सौ शरद ऋतुओं तक जीवित रहे।",
  "english": "Homage to you, O King Varuṇa; let there be homage to your wrath, for you, O fierce one, have noted all deceit. I send forth a thousand others together; may this one of yours live a hundred autumns.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Src 'hyu'gra' is hi + ugra with avagraha as printed. sṷvāmi in src stands for suvāmi. 'sahasram anyān pra suvāmi sākam' is obscure: 'I send forth a thousand others together (with him)' is the most literal reading. 'Namas te ... astu manyave' may also be read 'homage be to you, to your wrath'. jīvāti taken as subjunctive of √jīv (doubtful form). 'This one' is not identified.",
  "confidence": "medium"
